course: dictionary
lesson: 9970
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Teacher» usually means a person whose job is to help pupils learn, at school or in a class. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: Look at the clues. In «Ruby didn't start it, the teacher never asked», the teacher is someone at school. In «Experience is the best teacher», there is no person at all: it means you learn a lot by doing things yourself.
explain: Context also shows how formal a word is. Pupils say «Miss» or «Sir» to a teacher in some countries, which is casual talk, while «educator» and «instructor» are stiff, formal words.
fact: A teacher is a person whose job is to help pupils learn.
fact: Anyone who teaches you something can be your teacher, like a swimming teacher.
fact: «Experience is the best teacher» means you learn a lot by doing things yourself.
fact: «Teacher's pet» teases a pupil the teacher likes; it is casual talk, not a formal word.
fact: «Educator», «instructor» and «the invigilator» (who watches an exam) are formal words for people who teach or supervise.
exercise: «A boy in Halifax squints at the board, and his teacher notices.» In this sentence, who is the teacher? | A school bell | A friend of his mum | *A person at school whose job is to help him learn | A doctor who gives eye tests
exercise: «Experience is the best teacher» means what? | Experience is a job at school | The best teachers are the oldest | *You learn a lot by doing things yourself | Only old people know things
exercise: Which word is the stiff, formal word for a teacher? | Teacher's pet | *Instructor | Sir | Miss
test: In «Miss said I should try again», who is Miss? | A teacher who is always late | *A teacher, called Miss by the pupils | A type of exam | A girl who missed the bus
test: Which word is the formal name for the person who watches pupils during an exam? | *The invigilator | Supply teacher | Old dragon | Teacher's pet
exam: In «a teacher hands Everett a note in front of everyone», what is the teacher doing? | Writing a poem | Ringing the school bell | Going home early | *Giving something to a pupil
